<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deshastha Brahmin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Deshastha <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> Brahmin community of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-plateau">Deccan plateau</a>, the Desh, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>. They supplied many of the administrators, accountants and scholars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state, and several Maratha ministerial families, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv">Pant Sachivs</a> of Bhor, were Deshasthas. The saint-poets Eknath and Ramdas belonged to the community.</p></div>
